guous()\n\ncases = [\n    (1, 64, 512, 8, 64, 1.05, 5.0),\n    (1, 128, 640, 10, 64, 1.1, 4.0),\n    (1, 128, 1280, 20, 64, 1.15, 3.0),\n    (1, 256, 1280, 20, 64, 1.05, 7.5),\n    (1, 256, 640, 10, 64, 1.2, 5.0),\n    (2, 128, 512, 8, 64, 1.0, 5.0),\n]\n\nvariants = [\n    (\\\"ref\\\", ref),\n    (\\\"current\\\", current),\n    (\\\"combined\\\", opt_combined),\n]\n\ngeo = [1.0] * (len(variants) - 1)\ncnt = 0\n\nfor B, L, C, H, D, alpha, beta in cases:\n    torch.manual_seed(42)\n    x = torch.randn(B, L, C)\n    wq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    wk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    wv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    \n    ref_out = ref(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n    times = []\n    failed = []\n    for name, fn in variants:\n        ms = bench_median(lambda: fn(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta), n=25)\n        times.append(ms)\n        if name \"'!= \"ref\":\n            out = fn(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n            diff = (out - ref_out).abs().max().item()\n            maxe = ref_out.abs().max().item()\n            tol = 3e-5 + 3e-4 * maxe\n            if diff > tol:\n                failed.append(f\"{name}:{diff:.2e}\")\n    \n    label = f\"B{B}L{L}C{C}H{H}\"\n    print(f\"{label:18s}  ref={times[0]:7.2f}ms  \", end=\"\")\n    for j in range(1, len(variants)):\n        r = times[j] / times[0]\n        geo[j-1] *= r\n        print(f\"{variants[j][0]}={r:.4f}  \", end=\"\")\n    if failed:\n        print(f\"  FAIL: {failed}\")\n    else:\n        print()\n    cnt += 1\n\nprint(f\"'\"\\\\nGeometric mean ratio (vs ref):\\\")\nfor j in range(1, len(variants)):\n    print(f\\\"  {variants[j][0]:20s}: {geo[j-1]**(1/cnt):.4f}\\\")\nPYEOF\npython /tmp/bench_stable.py\"","aggregated_output":"B1L64C512H8         ref=  15.66ms  current=0.2963  combined=0.2961  \nB1L128C640H10       ref=  26.58ms  current=0.4803  combined=0.5343  \nB1L128C1280H20      ref=  87.67ms  current=0.4306  combined=0.4311  \nB1L256C1280H20      ref= 229.93ms  current=0.4661  combined=0.5044  \nB1L256C640H10       ref=  61.01ms  current=0.7392  combined=0.7236  \nB2L128C512H8        ref=  27.72ms  current=0.4735  combined=0.4727  \n\nGeometric mean ratio (vs ref):\n  current             : 0.4641\n  combined            : 0.4769\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"Let me try a more radical approach: compute q@k^T differently and explore whether we can fuse the Gram matrix computation with something else.\n\nActually, let me try an important optimization: precompute `logits.transpose(-1,-2)` once, and compute p1 more efficiently. Also, let me try using `torch.addmm` style operations.\n\nWait, I have another idea. The biggest chunk is still projection (40%). What if we can compute `p_mix @ v` directly from q,k,v without computing full p_mix? No, we need p_mix for the norm computation anyway.\n\nLet me try a different angle: compute `logits` as `(q * inv_sqrt_d) @ k.transpose(-1,-2)` — is that faster than `(q @ k.T) * inv_sqrt_d`? Probably not meaningful.\n\nActually, let me try something more impactful: can we compute `p0 @ v` and `p1 @ v` separately, then compute y = (1-beta)*y0 + beta*y1? We'd need two p@v matmuls instead of one. But that's still small compared to other costs.\n\nWait — for the alpha == 1.0 case, p1 = p0, so p_mix = p0, and ratio = 1.0. Our current fast path handles this correctly. Good.\n\nLet me think about what the \"round 9\" approach was — the one that achieved 0.4628. Let me re-read:\n> Key insight: the norm computation uses p1@G and p_mix@G (two separate L² matmuls per head). Since p_mix = (1-β)·p0 + β·p1, we can compute normm_sq from p0, p1 and their cross, saving one large p@G multiplication.\n\nWait, that's the \"round 9\" that got 0.4628. But my current code already uses two p@G multiplications (p1@G and pmG). The round 9 version supposedly used p0@G + p1@G + cross to avoid p_mix@G, which is still 2 matmuls.\n\nHmm, but wait — maybe the previous round had a 3-matmul approach and they went to 2? Let me re-read the problem spec more carefully.\n\nActually I think my current solution already IS the round-9 solution essentially. Let me try to squeeze more out of it.\n\nKey remaining cost breakdown (largest case):\n- Projection: ~41ms (36%)\n- p1 softmax: ~19ms (17%)  \n- p1 @ G: ~16ms (14%)\n- p0 softmax: ~13ms (11%)\n- p_mix @ G: ~12ms (10%)\n- logits q@k^T: ~4ms (4%)\n- G = x@x^T: ~4ms (3%)\n- p_mix @ v: ~4ms (3%)\n\nFor a total improvement, the projection is the biggest target. Let me think about whether we can reduce projection cost.\n\nWe have: x is (B*L, C), we need q, k, v each (B, H, L, D).\n- x @ wq.T = (BL, HD) → reshape (B, L, H, D) → permute (B, H, L, D)\n- Same for k, v.\n\nWhat if we use `torch.nn.functional.linear` instead? Probably same speed.\n\nWhat about combining projections more cleverly? Since the weights have shape (H, D, C), we could reshape to (H*D, C) and do three multiplications. We're already doing that.\n\nWait — what if we could avoid the permute entirely? The logits q@k^T needs q as (B, H, Lq, D) and k as (B, H, Lk, D). What if q and k are stored as (B, L, H, D) and we use einsum for logits?\n\nLet me try: `logits = torch.einsum(\"bqhd,bkhd->bhqk\", q_blhd, k_blhd)`. We know einsum is slower from microbench but maybe it avoids the permutation cost.\n</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"yield_time_ms\">\n\nLet me try a few more approaches focusing on the projection cost, which is the biggest remaining chunk.\n<parameter name=\"yield_time_ms\">\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat << 'PYEOF' > /tmp/bench_proj.py\nimport time, math, torch\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\ndef bench_median(fn, n=30, warmup=5):\n    for _ in range(warmup):\n        fn()\n    times = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        fn()\n        times.append(time.process_time_ns() - t0)\n    import statistics\n    return statistics.median(times) / 1e6\n\n# Test projection strategies for various sizes\ncases = [\n    (1, 64, 512, 8, 64),\n    (1, 128, 640, 10, 64),\n    (1, 128, 1280, 20, 64),\n    (1, 256, 1280, 20, 64),\n    (1, 256, 640, 10, 64),\n    (2, 128, 512, 8, 64),\n]\n\nprint(\\\"Projection-only benchmarks (ms):\\\")\nprint(f\\\"{'case':18s}  {'separate':>10s}  {'fused_cat':>10s}  {'einsum_q':>10s}\\\")\n\nfor B, L, C, H, D in cases:\n    torch.manual_seed(0)\n    x = torch.randn(B, L, C)\n    wq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    wk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    wv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n    \n    # Strategy 1: 3 separate matmuls + reshape + permute\n    def sep():\n        q = (xr @ wq.reshape(H*D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n        k = (xr @ wk.reshape(H*D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n        v = (xr @ wv.reshape(H*D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n        return q, k, v\n    \n    # Strategy 2: fused cat along HD dim\n    def fused_cat():\n        W = torch.cat([wq.reshape(H*D, C), wk.reshape(H*D, C), wv.reshape(H*D, C)], dim=0)\n        proj = xr @ W.T\n        proj_ = proj.reshape(B, L, 3*H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n        return proj_[:, 0:H, :, :], proj_[:, H:2*H, :, :], proj_[:, 2*H:3*H, :, :]\n    \n    # Strategy 3: einsum (just for q as reference - slow)\n    def einsum_q():\n        return torch.einsum(\\\"blc,hdc->bhld\\\", x, wq)\n    \n    t_sep = bench_median(sep)\n    t_fused = bench_median(fused_cat)\n    t_ein = bench_median(einsum_q)\n    \n    print(f\\\"B{B}L{L}C{C}H{H:2d}  {t_sep:10.3f}  {t_fused:10.3f}  {t_ein:10.3f}\\\")\n\n# Check correctness of fused\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\nx = torch.randn(B, L, C)\nwq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nxr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n\nq_ref = (xr @ wq.reshape(H*D, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\nW = torch.cat([wq.reshape(H*D, C), wk.reshape(H*D, C), wv.reshape(H*D, C)], dim=0)\nproj = xr @ W.T\nproj_ = proj.reshape(B, L, 3*H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\nq_fused = proj_[:, 0:H, :, :]\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nFused q diff: {(q_ref - q_fused).abs().max():.2e}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"Fused q contiguous: {q_fused.is_contiguous()}\\\")\nprint(f\\\"Sep q contiguous: {q_ref.is_contiguous()}\\\")\nPYEOF\npython /tmp/bench_proj.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
